60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Option B, the rotating location, feels the most fair. No one is stuck with it forever.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I like Option C. It keeps the point where it is, but the narrow window might help with the smell and the noise.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option C is the most logical. It minimizes the filing work and the time cost for each of us.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,I want Option B! Moving the bin is like a game. It is fair because everyone gets a turn.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Option C is wise. It addresses the root of the waste, the open bags, without the cost of a new structure.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Shizue, the narrow window might be hard to keep. What if someone forgets?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"We can remind each other. We are neighbours, after all. I think we can manage it with kindness.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,The filing for Option C is minimal. It is the most efficient use of our time and energy.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"If we forget, we can just move it! Option B is more fun and more fair.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"Forgetting is human, Kenji. But a shared responsibility, like Option C, builds a stronger bond than a rotation.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I hear you, Servas. A shared responsibility is good. But I still worry about the fairness of the location.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I think we can find a balance. Let's try Option C first. If it does not work, we can look at B.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I agree with Shizue. Option C is the most practical starting point. It is the least disruptive.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,"I am still for B, but I will listen. If C makes the bags closed, maybe it is okay.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,Let us begin with the simplest change that addresses the waste. Option C is that change.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I will vote for Option C. It is a step towards a better, more connected neighbourhood.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I will vote for Option C. I believe in our ability to care for each other and the space we share.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I will vote for Option C. It is the most logical and efficient solution for our time.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Rin,,"I will vote for Option C. If it means closed bags and no more open mess, I am in!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,I will vote for Option C. It is a path of shared care and mindful living.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
